# How GitHub reads this repo.
#
# Two problems without this file:
#
#  1. The language bar said "CSS". The theme files are bigger than the
#     tutorials, and GitHub excludes Markdown from language stats by
#     default, so the actual content of the repo was invisible while
#     generated styling dominated. Anyone landing here saw a CSS project.
#
#  2. Generated files showed up as large diffs in pull requests. Someone
#     fixing a typo in a tutorial does not want 148 lines of synced
#     tokens.css in their review.
#
# linguist-generated hides a file from stats AND collapses it in diffs.

# --- the point of the repo: count the tutorials ---
*.md    linguist-detectable=true
*.mdx   linguist-detectable=true

# --- generated, synced from the website repo by `npm run sync:brand` ---
src/styles/tokens.css   linguist-generated=true
src/assets/logo.png     linguist-generated=true binary
public/logo.png         linguist-generated=true binary
public/logo-lockup.png  linguist-generated=true binary
public/favicon.png      linguist-generated=true binary

# --- generated by scripts/make-og.mjs ---
public/og.png           linguist-generated=true binary
brand/og-template.html  linguist-generated=true

# --- lockfile ---
package-lock.json       linguist-generated=true

# --- keep line endings sane across contributors ---
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
